*> Implementation test of the density function evaluator (core/src/density.cob; T0416; docs/protocol/10 sections 4.1 to 4.3):
*> every node type of the overworld terrain data on the fixture tree core/tests/fixtures/density (arithmetic,
*> unary functions, squeeze, clamp, lerp with alpha 0 and 1, range choice, gradients on three axes with a descending
*> one, noise nodes with shifts and a noise defined with normalisation disabled, the three shift nodes, splines with
*> nested splines and both linear extensions, interpolated cells at a corner and inside a cell, the blending
*> constants, the beardifier, old_blended_noise and find_top_surface) bit for bit at eleven positions each. Expected values: an independent evaluator of the
*> same JSON written in Python from the section (float32 steps by struct rounding). A node of a type this evaluator does not know (end_outer_islands) and
*> a noise the data does not define evaluate to 0.
